From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lewis Gibson <12851394+lewisgibson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:23:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Enable /team with thread safe scoreboard teams

/team was disabled because the scoreboard is world global state shared by all
regions. Enable it, for the team subcommands only (scoreboard, teammsg and the
Bukkit scoreboard API stay disabled).

The invariant: a team, its members and its options are only ever observed
consistently, by any thread, and every online player's client sees each change
exactly once, in the order it was made.

How it holds:
- The team maps of Scoreboard are ConcurrentHashMaps and PlayerTeam#players is a
  concurrent set, because region threads read them (Entity#getTeam, display
  names, collision rules) while /team writes them. The option fields of
  PlayerTeam are volatile. Entity#getTeam, which Folia had stubbed to return null,
  reads them again, so selectors, collision rules, friendly fire and death
  messages see the teams.
- All mutation, together with the packets that announce it, happens under
  Scoreboard#teamLock, so concurrent /team commands, from rcon on the global
  region or from a player on its own region, cannot interleave their packets
  differently from their changes.
- A player used to receive the teams in PlayerList#updateEntireScoreboard, which
  Folia had disabled, so players that joined after a team existed never saw it.
  ServerScoreboard#syncTeamsTo sends the current teams to a player that has just
  joined and been added to the player list, under teamLock, and marks its
  connection as synced. Team changes are sent only to synced connections, so a
  change either happened before the snapshot, and is in it, or after it, and is
  broadcast to the player.
- Joining a team that another command removed after this one resolved it does
  nothing, and the scoreboard is saved from a snapshot taken under teamLock.

